The failure starts at ts-station-service and climbs through its callers to the user-facing dashboard. I have enough to write the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-station-service",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_failed",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-station-service' AND span_name='SELECT station' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 3",
          "claim": "Station's own 'SELECT station' DB spans now mostly end in Error at about 30,000 ms p95, versus about 4 ms normally."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT time, metric, count, sum/NULLIF(count,0) avg_wait_ms, max FROM abnormal_metrics_histogram WHERE metric='db.client.connections.wait_time' AND service_name='ts-station-service' ORDER BY time",
          "claim": "JDBC connection wait time jumps from sub-millisecond to about 30,000 ms once the incident starts, and stays there."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT level, message, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-station-service' AND level IN ('SEVERE','ERROR','WARN') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "Station logs 'Unable to acquire JDBC Connection' and 'Communications link failure' errors repeatedly during the incident."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-station-service",
      "to": "ts-basic-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
